NAME "/learn Slash Command Alignment"
WINDOW 100 30

# TARGET pigasus, not both.
#
# The reference half of this scenario needs a signed-in agy: `/learn` starts a
# model turn, and an unauthenticated agy stops at the OAuth prompt before any
# turn begins (verified: `HOME=$(mktemp -d) agy -p '/learn'` prints
# "Authentication required"). The reference account is suspended, so the
# two-binary diff cannot run on this machine.
#
# What that leaves is still worth asserting, and it is the half that can
# regress: the *clone's* command must echo, start a turn, and send the
# reference's 2,178-byte instruction. The instruction itself is pinned
# byte-for-byte by `go run ./devutils/wirealign test` (the /learn entry in
# devutils/wirealign/slashprompts.go), so this scenario covers the TUI
# behaviour and wirealign covers the bytes. Flip this to `both` on a machine
# with a signed-in reference to get the pixel diff too.
TARGET pigasus

SETTINGS {"showTips":false}

# /learn sends a prompt, so the model answers it. The mock answer is short and
# deliberately generic: the parity claim here is about what the command puts on
# the wire and on screen, not about the model's reply.
MOCK_TURN
  THOUGHT "Reviewing the recent corrections before proposing a rule..." TOKENS 60 DELAY 100ms
  TEXT "I found one reusable correction in this session. Proposal written to learning_proposal.md; review it before I touch any rule file."
  USAGE PROMPT 9000 CANDIDATES 20 THOUGHTS 60
  FINISH STOP

BOOT
WAIT_READY 10s

# 1. The echo. Every prompt-sending command echoes its canonical name as
#    "> /learn"; the cycle-167 shape appended to session state and printed a
#    fixed line instead. One Enter is enough: the picker submits a command the
#    composer already spells out in full.
TYPE "/learn"
ENTER

EXPECT_TEXT "> /learn" 10s
SNAPSHOT "01_learn_echo"

# 2. The turn actually runs. The reference starts a turn, so a reply has to
#    appear; a command that only recorded a note would leave the transcript
#    without a response.
EXPECT_TEXT "learning_proposal.md" 20s
SNAPSHOT "02_learn_turn_complete"

# 3. /learn takes an argument: the text after the command is prepended to the
#    instruction rather than dropped.
TYPE "/learn the API endpoint must be read from config, never hardcoded"
ENTER

EXPECT_TEXT "> /learn" 10s
EXPECT_TEXT "learning_proposal.md" 20s
SNAPSHOT "03_learn_with_argument"

DIFF
CLEANUP
